    "lawCode": "Add §399-eee, Gen Bus L",
    "lawSection": "General Business Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S2464A\n\nSPONSOR: PERSAUD\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the general business law, in relation to requiring car\nwashes to disclose when promotions expire\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nRequires car washes to disclose pricing information associated with\npromotions.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 requires car washes to disclose pricing information when\nadvertising a promotion. It also requires them to post notice in a visi-\nble place.\n\nSection 2 provides an effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nA 2023 consumer alert published by New York Attorney General Letitia\nJames is the latest report in previous years of discriminatory pricing\npractices in which consumers are charged increased prices under the\nguise of advertised \"specials.\" Such illegal practices erode the trust\nof consumers in the services rendered by law-abiding businesses. This\nbill provides additional protections to consumers in New York State by\nrequiring clear communication of pricing information so that they can\nmake informed financial decisions.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2022/2023: S2464 Referred to Consumer Protection Committee\n\n \nFISCAL IMPACT ON THE STATE:\n\nNone noted.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the thirtieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law.\n",
