    "lawCode": "Add §399-eee, Gen Bus L",
    "lawSection": "General Business Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S2464B\n\nSPONSOR: PERSAUD\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the general business law, in relation to requiring car\nwashes to disclose when promotions expire\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo provide additional transparency and protections to consumers by\nrequiring car washes to disclose pricing information associated with\npromotions.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of the bill adds a new § 399-eee to the general business\nlaw. This would require car washes to clearly state when a promotion\nwill expire and the costs associated with such promotions. Car washes\nwill also be required to conspicuously post notice of such information\non a board or other visible place in view of consumers when advertising\na promotion, including online if advertised there as well. Violations\nare punishable by a civil penalty of up to five hundred dollars for each\nviolation.\n\nSection two of the bill provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nA 2023 consumer alert published by New York Attorney General Letitia\nJames is the latest report of discriminatory pricing practices in which\nconsumers are charged increased prices under the guise of advertised\n\"specials.\" Such illegal practices erode the trust of consumers in the\nservices rendered by law-abiding businesses. This bill provides addi-\ntional protections to consumers in New York State by requiring clear\ncommunication of pricing information so that they can make informed\nfinancial decisions.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2021-22-: S.9259 - Referred to Consumer Protection\n\n \nFISCAL IMPACT ON THE STATE:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the thirtieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law.\n",
